03:52Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112607","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112607","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112607.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112607.patch","merged_at":"2025-11-18T20:03:52Z"},"body":"Follow-up to #112267\r\nSupersedes #112605\r\n\r\n*Bugsquad edit:*\r\n- Fixes #112655\r\n- Fixes #112863\r\n\r\nForcing no skeleton path has caused problems as expected, so this PR takes a bit different approach.\r\n- When opening a project created before 4.6 (based on `features` setting), `default_parent_skeleton_in_mesh_instance_3d` is set to true\r\n- Running the project upgrade tool will set the setting to false and fix the scenes\r\n\r\nThis takes away some advantages of #112267, as users need to be aware of the compat option to make use of it (unless they create a new project). I added a note in the docs and we should probably make a prominent note in the update blog post for next version.\r\n\r\nPlease test and provide a reproduction project if there are still problems. I got some weird results when testing this (although it seems to fix the problem).","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","